WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.534
-Betty, welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.367
-Thanks for having me. -Oh, please. I appreciate this.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.968
We just had Ice-T on, and we were talking --

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.868
It's kind of a rite of passage for New York actors

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.667
to be on "Law &amp; Order."

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:12.968
-Yes, yeah. Yeah.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.067
For, like, the first couple of years of my career,

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.901
it was only theater and "Law &amp; Order."

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.968
So I did an order of "SVU."

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.868
I was a pedophile with vocal fry.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.534
-Congratulations. -Thank you.

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:24.968
And I was a lesbian --

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.801
-No spinoff -- No spinoff from that one.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.701
-I can't believe it. I'm still waiting on that call.

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.033
-Yeah. -And I was a lesbian with acne

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.734
on "the mothership," we called it,

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.968
just the normal "Law &amp; Order." -Oh, interesting.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.934
You were multiple different -- Were you ever a dead body?

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.334
-I was a dead body on "Criminal Intent."

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:43.501
And then, within the same year, I was an alive person.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.701
-Same season? -Yes, same season.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.634
They were like, "No one cares. No one remembers you."

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:53.067
Excellent. But I was --

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.400
The dead body, I was Fran Drescher's daughter,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.834
which is an honor, but I don't know about that casting.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:01.200
-Yeah. Interesting. -But, yeah, I was found --

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.367
True fans will know.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.567
I was found naked in an oil drum.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:07.434
Vincent D'Onofrio, like, found my naked dead body.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.334
-So sorry to hear that. -Yeah.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.467
And we filmed it where --

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.667
I don't know if they still film "SVU" there,

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.067
but we filmed it outside Chelsea Piers.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.834
-Yep. -And they had all these

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.601
modesty screens because I was going to be naked

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.567
and crumpled up in this oil barrel.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.167
So they had all these screens

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:27.267
protecting me from the crew on the Chelsea Piers side.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.534
And then as I was taking off my robe, I was like,

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.100
"Oh, the West Side Highway."

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.133
Like -- vroom!

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.200
-Every human being, that's -- Yeah.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.968
-"Wait! What's happening?"

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:40.133
-This was the time before, you know, intimacy coordinators.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.667
They were like, "We're losing light. Take the robe off."

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.801
-Yeah. And then you just had to be --

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:47.801
-And then -- So, we filmed the scene of them

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.234
zipping up the body bag at a different location

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:51.834
at, like, a remote beach.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.267
And this is my first job ever.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:57.100
And I remember them zipping up the body bag.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.567
Vincent D'Onofrio had, like,

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.300
a grumbly scene over my body bag.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.968
And I just had to sort of be in there.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.501
And then they called cut.

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.367
They're like, "That's lunch, guys! Great day!"

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.234
And I hear, like, footsteps on gravel

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.868
getting farther and farther away,

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:11.367
van doors closing.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.534
And then, like, 10 seconds goes by.

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:16.767
I hear one far-away P.A. being like, "Oh, my God."

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.167
And footsteps coming towards me.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:21.534
Like, unzips. Sunlight in my face. Yeah.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:23.834
"Let's get you out of there!"

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:27.200
-That's really funny. Like, "Hello! Help! Hello?"

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.601
-No, I didn't want to be high-maintenance.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.300
I wanted to work again in the same season.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.567
-It's your first job.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.067
You don't want to ruin the scene, of course.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.067
-No. -You've been on our show before,

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.100
but I just heard you have a -- we met each other before that

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.467
I might not have known about.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.167
Back in this building in the '90s.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:44.400
-In this building in 1998. What a time it was.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.200
I was 12 years old,

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.667
and my brain was a castle of delusions

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:52.234
because I was so angry that I wasn't a child star.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.601
My parents wouldn't let me be a child actor.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.601
But we got tickets to "SNL."

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.634
And I was like, "Well, maybe fate will have it

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:03.701
that I get discovered in the audience of 'SNL.'"

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.968
-Lorne Michaels might just see you in the audience and be like,

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.133
"You have something."

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.467
-Really anyone. -Anyone.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.033
-Time would stop, and I'd become

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:13.234
Millie Bobby Brown meets Daniel Day Lewis at once.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.434
You know, finally. -Yes.

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:17.834
-And Jennifer Love Hewitt was the host,

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.667
who I was obsessed with.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:23.501
She had everything I didn't -- IMDb page and cleavage.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.501
I was praying for both.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.667
And she was dating Carson Daly at the time.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:29.767
-Of course.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.400
-They were, like, the hottest couple.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.734
He hosted "TRL." -Oh, it's massive.

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:35.567
They were the it couple.

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:38.968
-Yeah, like the Tom Holland and Zendaya of the day.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.601
-Yes. -It was remarkable.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.100
And I sat right behind him.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.167
And I was like, "This is fate. I'm behind Carson Daly."

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:46.367
He's going to turn around --

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:49.634
'Cause, I guess, in my head he was the --

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:52.901
Like, "TRL" and "Guys and Dolls" was my world,

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:55.734
so I was like, "Carson Daly probably runs MGM.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:58.567
He'll turn around and see me and make me a star."

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:00.100
-Yeah. "You got something, kid."

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.801
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah. And I'd have the contract by Monday.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.367
-Yeah. -Didn't happen.

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:09.300
My strategy was to -- This was, you know, before COVID.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.968
I was like, "I'll just cough on the back of his neck."

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.734
Like... -I'm sorry.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:18.100
So your plan is to cough on the back of Carson Daly's neck.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.267
-Yeah.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.601
-To the point where it would annoy him maybe?

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:23.133
-Well, he'd be like, "Who is -- who IS that?"

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:29.467
-That's such a great delivery.

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:31.067
"Hey, who is -- Hey, who IS that?"

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.267
-"Oh, my God. Yeah.

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:35.067
Can we get the house lights up? This is a star."

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:38.033
-I'm so happy to hear that. That's a very fun story.

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:40.100
And look at what you've done now. Oh, my gosh.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.167
Nominated for Emmys, and you're just crushing it.

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.767
I want to talk about "Roar" quickly.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:47.634
"Roar" is -- It's on apple TV Plus.

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:50.734
And every episode tells a different woman's story.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:51.968
-Yeah.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.934
-This story -- They're all super interesting.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:56.267
This one is called "The Woman Who Was Kept on a Shelf."

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:57.334
-Yeah.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.234
-And you literally are up on a shelf.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:02.434
-Yes, so this was created by Liz Flahive and Carly Mensch,

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.200
who created "Glow" and we worked together on "Nurse Jackie."

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.701
So they kind of know that my personal brand

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.934
is playing woman who are not okay.

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:12.033
And this is no exception.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:16.467
It's kind of like a fantastical allegory for the trophy wife,

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:19.234
and I play a woman who lives on her husband's shelf

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:22.033
and goes slowly insane. -Yeah, I love it.

00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:24.467
I think the whole season, the whole idea --

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:27.234
every single episode is a different story of a woman.

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:29.100
-Yeah, yeah. -And it's -- it's well done.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.934
-Nicole Kidman, Cynthia Erivo, Alison Brie.

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:33.801
The love of my life. -Alison Brie!

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.934
Yeah, she was here talking about it. It was great.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.934
I want to talk about "Gaslit" now.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.701
This is your other show. This show is --

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:43.567
Basically everyone's saying it's Julia Roberts' return,

00:05:43.567 --> 00:05:45.200
kind of. We haven't seen Julia in a while.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.634
-Her performance is insane. She's incredible.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.200
-She is incredible. -Incredible.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.501
-Yeah, and --

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:52.100
have you ever worked with Julia before or met her?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.367
-I had never -- No. I'd never worked with her.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:56.667
It's so unfortunate.

00:05:56.667 --> 00:06:00.300
I, in this series, play Mo Dean, who was a real person,

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.033
wife of John Dean, who was in the White House Counsel.

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:04.801
And Mo Dean had -- -We have a picture of her.

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:07.834
-Yeah, so she has white blonde hair.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.501
And I do not, against all odds.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:14.267
And I wore this wig that was this platinum blond,

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.601
almost like Daenerys Targaryen wig.

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:19.968
And the process was -- It wasn't just like you pop the wig on.

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:22.100
Like, they had to put a bald cap

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.667
and paint it white and then put the wig on.

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:27.467
And I was like, "Please, Lord, don't let the first time

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:30.534
I meet Julia Roberts be halfway through

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:34.033
when I look like a White Walker in a nursing home."

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:35.667
Like, with two tendrils coming.

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:37.534
It looked insane, insane, insane.

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:39.868
I once FaceTimed my husband in that bald cap,

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.367
and he was like, "Never do this again."

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:46.434
And, of course, I met her when I was in that exact phase.

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:48.501
Like, "Hi, girl-legend. I normally don't look like this.

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:50.667
I'm so sorry. This is terrifying."

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:53.234
-And she's just the most fun. -Yeah, she's incredible.

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:54.734
-Yeah, and then knocks it out of the park.

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:57.067
-I want to show everyone a clip. Here's Betty Gilpin in "Gaslit."

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:58.200
Take a look.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.400
-Wait, please. -John.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.067
-Please. -You seem very nice.

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:04.834
Do you know what it is? I am looking for a man.

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:07.334
And I can't waste my time with little boys anymore.

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:08.634
-I know I was a [bleep] the other night.

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:10.067
-Mm-hmm. -But I wanna make it up to you.

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.400
There's this fundraiser next weekend,

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.868
and everyone who's anyone in D.C. is going to be there.

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:16.133
-You want to take me to a Republican fundraiser?

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:18.300
-It'll be great material for your novel.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.734
And, besides, we don't have to talk to anybody.

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:21.734
We can just sit in the corner all night,

00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:23.267
drinking John Mitchell's Scotch.

00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:27.033
-Uh, John Mitchell? Martha Mitchell's husband?

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:28.868
-Yeah, why? You like him?

00:07:28.868 --> 00:07:32.100
-She's completely insane. I love her.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.300
-Ooh! Betty Gilpin!

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.868
"Gaslit" premieres this Sunday at 8:00 p.m. on Starz.

00:07:38.868 --> 00:07:40.968
I love you, bud. Come back whenever you want.

